WEBVTT

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:23.730
Take a key and lock her up.

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:28.900
Lock her up, lock her up.

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:35.030
Take a key and lock her up.

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:39.910
My fair lady.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:47.960
Sketching your dreams won't make them come true.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.960
It's something you fight for and turn into a reality.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:56.220
Who are you?

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.720
I came to set you free.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:28.960
Hi!

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:33.670
Well?

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:34.590
What?

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:37.510
What kind of trouble did you bring with you today?

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.260
Trouble?

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:45.970
Trouble's always afoot when you walk in here with a cheerful "Hi."

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.100
Not today it isn't.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.440
Well, why are you here then?

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:53.060
Well, I came to drop this off.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:56.940
A concert? Are you participating in it?

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.070
Yeah.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:03.160
I want you to hear me play.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.450
Why are you inviting me?

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:07.790
Is this some form of harassment?

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.710
Or perhaps this is your new method of blackmailing me?

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:12.880
You don't have to be that rude about it.

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.590
Well, if...

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:20.380
If I happen to be totally dying of boredom that day,

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:26.100
and if I just so happen to be within the vicinity, I might just drop by.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:29.560
Okay.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.400
Please stop by if you so happen to be dying of boredom and within the vicinity.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.610
I'll bring along your ticket tomorrow.

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:37.530
And don't forget to do something about your smile.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:39.110
It gives me the creeps.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:40.360
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:07.560
It'll all be over before you wake up.

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:37.000
I heard that this place was haunted, but none of the photographs I've taken show anything abnormal.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:02.610
Hey, are you okay?

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:06.950
Th-There's a ghost...

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:08.910
I'm scared.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.080
Save me!

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.790
Please, save me.

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:16.620
Don't worry. You're fine now.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.710
You want me to watch footage of a ghost caught on camera?

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:24.420
Yeah, that's right.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:27.470
That journalist handed it to us.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:34.730
It was filmed in a mansion where 4 people were murdered 15 years ago.

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:38.600
You mean the case where four family members were murdered, the Nanase Murders, right?

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:40.860
How did you know that?

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:43.480
Because the statute of limitations was recently abolished.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:48.320
As a result, unsolved cases like this are often talked about in the media nowadays.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:52.330
With regards to this case, a special investigation team has been formed

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:55.870
within the municipal police to arrest Takeda Shunsuke.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:06:00.290
Obviously, we expected that the Criminal Investigation Division's Unsolved Cases Special Investigation Unit

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:03.300
would be invited to join the investigation, but...

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.340
But you weren't.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:06.920
How did you know?

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:11.260
In addition, the one who made that decision was Miyagawa-san,

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:13.850
Goto-san's senior and the one who trained him.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:17.020
I finally get the full picture.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:26.400
You plan to find new clues from this footage and investigate it from a different angle?

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:27.950
Exactly!

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:31.870
Very well, I'll take a look.

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:33.620
Really?!

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:37.750
What are you so surprised about? You're the one who asked me for help.

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:40.920
Well, I figured you'd decline,

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:44.170
since there's nothing really that interesting about this case.

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:50.010
The woman who filmed this is Hoshino Yukiko-san.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:53.890
She's a script writer for a video production company in the city.

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:56.680
What's she doing right now?

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:01.650
She's hospitalized due to shock, but it's nothing serious.

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:06.730
She answered my questions with clarity, so I doubt she's been possessed.

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:10.700
You're really persuasive. I guess it comes from experience.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:16.120
Apparently she was researching locations while putting together a special television program on

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:19.790
the Nanase Murders which happened 15 years ago.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:24.340
This is the footage in question.

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:27.000
I had professionals look over it.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:32.220
There were no signs of video editing or the addition of computer graphics.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:33.970
Are you sure?

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:35.100
Yes, we're certain.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:36.510
Then I'll play it.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:41.940
I-I'll wait outside.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:45.440
Aren't you a fan of these kinds of things?

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:47.190
What are you scared of?

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:49.610
I don't know how to explain this...

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:51.490
It's.. er...

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:53.160
F-For example-

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:54.160
Ishii-san?

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:55.660
Yes!

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.540
I'm starting it.

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:58.790
O-Okay.

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:05.330
Yakumo-kun's not in.

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:14.970
What the hell is this?

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:17.350
It's been like this the whole time.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:20.470
She must've messed up the exposure settings.

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:25.230
She's a script writer. She's probably not good with technology.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:28.480
It continues on like this.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:30.650
Please fast forward it.

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:32.700
No, please don't.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:35.910
There's no use in watching it like this.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:38.700
How many years have you been a police officer?

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:39.740
What?

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:45.080
Why would you fast forward it when we don't even know where a clue might be hidden.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.750
That's true, but...

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:00.260
There!

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:06.480
Next is the living room.

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:08.150
There it is!

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:13.030
That was the voice of the lady filming it, idiot.

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:20.740
Your precious friend will die tonight.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:27.960
Please fast forward it.

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:30.710
Hey, are you sure?

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:33.840
How many years have you been a police officer?

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:37.470
It's a waste of time watching this thing.

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:40.260
You bastard...

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.470
It's around here.

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:01.490
This is the ghost in question.

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:03.660
H-Hey, Yakumo!

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:12.630
Yakumo-san?

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.520
That ghost is...

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:28.810
Probably...

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:40.200
No way, it's Yakumo-kun?

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:44.580
It's rare for you to call me, isn't it?

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:50.790
It's nothing really important, but I wanted to talk to you about your concert.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:55.210
Oh, I left your ticket in the Film Club's room.

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:57.880
I'm sorry, but I might not be able to make it.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:58.880
What?

00:10:58.880 --> 00:10:59.840
I'm sorry.

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:03.970
Hey, did something happen?

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:04.970
Not really.

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:06.020
Liar!

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:07.560
Something definitely happened!

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:08.980
How can you be so sure?

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:11.810
A woman's intuition.

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:15.980
I guess I can't trust your intuition then.

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:17.820
Also...

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:21.700
No, it's nothing.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:22.870
Wait.

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:25.240
Yakumo-kun, can we meet right now-

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:40.170
That Yakumo...

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:42.470
No matter how many times I call him, he doesn't answer.

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:47.100
Yakumo-shi didn't return after leaving the room yesterday, did he?

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:49.020
Yeah...

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:52.900
Captain Miyagawa!

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.440
Oh, it's you, Miya-san.

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:56.520
Ow!

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:00.030
You're free right now, right?

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:01.200
Nope.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:04.700
If I say you're free, then you're free.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:06.990
Don't talk back, idiot.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:13.460
Yakumo-kun hasn't been back.

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:39.480
Yakumo-kun, where did you go?

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:51.290
Is... my wife doing well?

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:56.290
Atsuko should've gone home already.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:57.710
You haven't seen her?

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:00.630
You should go home more often, you know.

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:09.350
I wonder what she's doing now...

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:14.850
I'm talking about Nanase Miyuki-chan, she was kidnapped during that incident.

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:17.230
It's been 15 years already.

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:19.690
She should be 24 or 25 now.

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:23.860
Well, that's if she's still alive.

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:28.990
That night, I heard about it on the police radio on my way home.

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:37.080
We'd received a report from the neighbors that a scream was heard from Nanase Kanji's residence.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:40.130
I reached the scene a little past midnight.

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:47.550
There was no response from the residents, so I entered the house alone.

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:06.360
The room was a pool of blood.

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:13.540
In the Nanase's house, Nanase Kanji, his son, Katsuaki, and both their wives had been killed.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:16.210
Then I heard a sound from the entrance.

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:19.670
When I got there, I found their daughter standing there.

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:22.170
Ten year-old Miyuki-chan.

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:24.630
She was completely unharmed.

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:27.510
But before I could take her into protective custody,

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:39.390
I was hit on the head, by someone who I believe to be the culprit, and lost consciousness.

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:45.480
When I regained consciousness, I was lying in a hospital bed.

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:49.820
If only I'd managed to arrest the culprit back then...

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:54.830
This case is unsolved because Miya-san messed up, eh?

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:54.830
[Note: A play on words by Goto - "unsolved cases" are called "Miyaokuri" or "Omiya-san."]

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.370
I can't sleep at night.

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:03.460
The suspect, Takeda, was a freelance journalist.

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:09.470
People say that he came under a huge amount of unjust pressure after he published that article

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:11.680
about the scandal that happened in the private middle school the Nanase family operated.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:16.520
As a result of that, he lost his job and people believed that he murdered them as payback.

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:21.440
I heard he was vilified.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:22.860
He must have just snapped.

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:29.490
But his articles have always sided with the weak.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:35.830
It doesn't fit the personality of someone who wrote as he did to go and do something like that.

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:38.540
And there's another thing.

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:44.380
Was that shadow I saw really Takeda's?

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:46.130
No, more importantly...

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:49.880
was it even human?

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:54.090
I can't really explain it,

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:58.970
but it wasn't human... It was something more terrifying.

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:02.810
I can't help but feel that...

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:09.400
But if you take into account his alibi and the physical evidence we have, it all points to Takeda.

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:12.740
All that's left is to arrest him.

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:15.160
You're absolutely right.

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:18.370
And that's why we're currently looking for Takeda.

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:21.290
Miya-san...

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:23.920
What?!

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:28.630
We're going to... investigate the Nanase residence... tonight?

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:30.880
Stop screaming like a girl.

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:33.130
Just the two of us?

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:35.840
Want me to ask for an entire police squad to accompany us?

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:39.770
Can we at least ask Yakumo-shi to accompany us?

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:44.690
I really do want to, but no matter how many times I call him, he doesn't answer.

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:47.860
In that case, let's go and investigate the scene now.

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:50.400
It's still light, okay?

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:52.530
I have other plans right now.

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:53.320
Other plans?

00:16:53.990 --> 00:17:00.450
We're going to interview Hoshino, the girl who filmed the footage of the ghost.

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.250
Excuse us.

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:05.460
Come in.

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:07.920
Excuse us for the intrusion.

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:11.510
Nice to meet you. We're the-

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:13.050
The police, right?

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:16.430
Hijikata-san called and said you'd be coming.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:18.680
Please cooperate with us.

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:20.470
Of course.

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:29.400
Y-You're...

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.280
Detective Goto, do you know each other?

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:40.450
No... she just reminds me of someone I know...

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:45.120
You know, like how they say there are seven people who resemble you in this world?

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:47.620
I think you're a tad wrong with that phrase.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:49.790
Shut up, just get on with the questioning!

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:50.710
Right!

00:17:55.510 --> 00:18:00.260
The two of us are really investigating this by ourselves, right?

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:04.020
What happened to Yakumo?

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:10.110
Did he start acting on his own because he knew who she was?

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:13.320
U-Um, Detective Goto?

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:14.860
What? Yeah.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:15.990
Let's go.

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:18.410
What's wrong?

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:20.780
Um... you see... I... er...

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:21.910
That's enough.

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:22.910
Ow!

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:29.040
Just wait there, you coward!

00:18:57.240 --> 00:18:58.150
Who's there?

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:13.960
D-Detective Goto...

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:19.800
Hello, is this the p-police?

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:22.760
P-P-Please help me!

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:39.950
Goto's disappearance is a terrible case.

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:46.120
I'll turn a blind eye to the fact that you didn't try and rescue him because you were afraid of a ghost.

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:49.870
But what are you still doing here?

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:53.000
Why aren't you out looking for Goto?

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:57.590
It's impossible for a coward like me.

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:13.440
I have a message for you from Atsuko-No, Goto's wife.

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:16.860
"Please take care of my husband."

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:19.860
Do you understand the meaning behind these words?

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:29.450
Listen, if anything happens to him, I will never forgive you.

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:50.770
Yakumo-kun, where did you disappear to?

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:57.310
Hello, is this Isshin-san?

00:20:57.310 --> 00:21:00.730
Um, is Yakumo-kun there?

00:21:54.410 --> 00:21:58.830
I was waiting for you, Yakumo. For you to come here.

00:22:00.630 --> 00:22:04.300
That video was a trap to lure you here.

00:22:05.630 --> 00:22:11.350
You're so smart. You must've noticed that it was filmed here, right?

00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:17.100
And my voice, we've spoken on the phone before, remember?

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:21.110
Who... are you?

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:24.570
I'm here to bring you into darkness.

00:22:26.440 --> 00:22:28.700
I love you, Yakumo.

00:22:32.370 --> 00:22:34.740
So much that I want to ruin you.
